# “Asking for Data”

<img src="https://images.code.org/5f49c06b5874c513ec0055162e10b53c-image-1770743675458.png" alt="simple diagram showing client app sending request to server and receiving response" width="650px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;border-radius:10px; ">

### **What Happens When an App Uses an API?**

When an app uses an API, it’s usually doing something like this:

- The **client app** sends a **request** asking for data  
- A **server** receives the request  
- The server sends back a **response** with the data  

This is how apps can show **live, up-to-date information** that changes over time.

